+/// Where in its range the next Table starts: a whole number of pages,
+/// under 2 MiB. A Table's lowest slots are its most used, and Tables
+/// that all started on 2 MiB boundaries would put those pages at the
+/// same address modulo 2 MiB, so in one set of the processor's
+/// second-level TLB, which holds far fewer than a program's dozens of
+/// Tables: each would evict the others, and every use of a Table's first
+/// page would walk the page tables. Started at different pages, they
+/// fall in different sets.
+/// The Table touches as many pages as it would from its range's start.
+fn colorOf() usize {
+    const k = table_colors.fetchAdd(1, .monotonic);
+    return (k *% color_stride % (huge_page / std.heap.page_size_min)) * std.heap.page_size_min;
